WEBVTT
1
00:00:00,537 --> 00:00:04,184
 I've been building software from an early age.

2
00:00:04,165 --> 00:00:06,480
 Although much of my earliest work

3
00:00:06,460 --> 00:00:09,720
 was created locally and is no longer available.

4
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:13,720
 My verifiable online journey dates back to 2014.

5
00:00:13,700 --> 00:00:17,719
 when I created my developer account on Kongregate,

6
00:00:17,699 --> 00:00:20,790
 at just 13 years old.

7
00:00:20,770 --> 00:00:22,798
 By then,

8
00:00:22,778 --> 00:00:26,393
 I had already been experimenting with game development for some time.

9
00:00:26,373 --> 00:00:30,392
 I began by creating games with Scratch.

10
00:00:30,372 --> 00:00:33,412
 GameMaker Studio and Construct 2

11
00:00:33,393 --> 00:00:35,961
 In 2017,

12
00:00:35,941 --> 00:00:39,454
 I published my first online game on Kongregate,

13
00:00:39,434 --> 00:00:41,698
 built with Construct 2,

14
00:00:41,678 --> 00:00:44,854
 marking my first public software release.

15
00:00:44,834 --> 00:00:47,318
 In 2018,

16
00:00:47,298 --> 00:00:51,115
 I transitioned from no-code and low-code game development

17
00:00:51,095 --> 00:00:53,123
 to writing code,

18
00:00:53,103 --> 00:00:55,975
 learning C++ fundamentals and

19
00:00:55,955 --> 00:00:59,772
 strengthening my understanding of computer science.

20
00:00:59,752 --> 00:01:03,332
 By 2020, I had started

21
00:01:03,312 --> 00:01:05,982
 sharing code publicly on Pastebin.

22
00:01:05,962 --> 00:01:08,158
 created my GitHub account,

23
00:01:08,138 --> 00:01:11,955
 and published a mobile application built with Sketchware

24
00:01:11,935 --> 00:01:13,980
 on itch.io.

25
00:01:13,960 --> 00:01:17,980
 In 2021, I expanded into web development by building

26
00:01:17,960 --> 00:01:20,241
 my first full-stack web application,

27
00:01:20,221 --> 00:01:22,468
 a Google Forms clone.

28
00:01:22,448 --> 00:01:24,477
 built with native PHP,

29
00:01:24,457 --> 00:01:27,126
 MySQL, and vanilla JavaScript.

30
00:01:27,106 --> 00:01:29,539
 and deployed to Heroku.

31
00:01:29,519 --> 00:01:32,695
 Followed by an anonymous messaging

32
00:01:32,675 --> 00:01:35,361
 platform inspired by Sarahah.

33
00:01:35,341 --> 00:01:38,955
 These projects marked the beginning of my journey

34
00:01:38,935 --> 00:01:41,318
 into modern web development.

35
00:01:41,298 --> 00:01:45,317
 In 2022, while still a university student,

36
00:01:45,297 --> 00:01:49,317
 I began working as a full-time frontend developer,

37
00:01:49,297 --> 00:01:53,316
 turning a lifelong passion into a profession.

38
00:01:53,296 --> 00:01:55,324
 I graduated in

39
00:01:55,304 --> 00:01:57,973
 2023 with a Bachelor's.

40
00:01:57,953 --> 00:02:01,332
 degree in Physics from the Faculty of Science,

41
00:02:01,312 --> 00:02:03,694
 Kafr El-Sheikh University.

42
00:02:03,674 --> 00:02:06,985
 My journey from game development to software engineering has

43
00:02:06,965 --> 00:02:09,414
 shaped my approach to continuous learning

44
00:02:09,395 --> 00:02:13,161
 problem solving, and building products that

45
00:02:13,140 --> 00:02:15,169
 create real value.

46
00:02:15,149 --> 00:02:17,717
 The journey continues,

47
00:02:17,697 --> 00:02:21,666
 but I just wanted to share how it started!

